    ],
    answer: 'In the sixth year after the Hijrah the Prophet ﷺ set out toward Makkah to perform \'Umrah and the Quraysh tried to stop him. Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan reported: the Prophet ﷺ set out at the time of Hudaybiyyah, his camel sat down, and he said she was stopped by the One who stopped the elephant; he said that if the Quraysh asked for anything that honoured Allah\'s sanctities he would grant it (Sahih al-Bukhari 2731).\n\nHe told their envoy Budayl that he had come to perform \'Umrah and not to fight, and offered a truce. The long hadith goes on to the talks that followed.\n\nSurah Al-Fath opens with Allah saying: We have given you a clear victory (Qur\'an 48:1). Many scholars say it was revealed after Hudaybiyyah, and that the truce opened the way for the later conquest of Makkah.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 2731; Qur\'an 48:1.\n[GO:/stories]',
