    answer: 'The Muhajirun are the Companions who left Makkah for Allah\'s sake; the Ansar (\'helpers\') are the people of Madinah who gave them shelter and support.\n\nThe Qur\'an praises both: the poor emigrants who were driven from their homes (Qur\'an 59:8), and those who made their home in Madinah, love those who came to them and prefer them over themselves even in need (Qur\'an 59:9). It also speaks of the foremost of the emigrants and the helpers (Qur\'an 9:100).\n\nAnas reported the Prophet ﷺ saying: love of the Ansar is a sign of faith and hatred of the Ansar is a sign of hypocrisy (Sahih al-Bukhari 17).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 59:8, 59:9, 9:100; Sahih al-Bukhari 17.\n[GO:/stories]',
