    answer: 'Zuhd is not owning less for its own sake; it is keeping the world in your hand and not in your heart.\n\nIbn Umar reported: the Prophet ﷺ took hold of his shoulder and said to be in this world as if a stranger or a traveller (Sahih al-Bukhari 6416). Ibn Umar used to say that in the evening you should not expect the morning, nor in the morning the evening, and to take from your health for your sickness and from your life for your death.\n\nThe Qur\'an reminds that the life of this world is only play and amusement while the home of the Hereafter is better for those who fear Allah (Qur\'an 6:32).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 6416; Qur\'an 6:32.\n[GO:/hadith]',
