    answer: 'The days of Tashriq are the three days after the Day of Sacrifice (the 11th, 12th and 13th of Dhul Hijjah).\n\nNubayshah al-Hudhali reported the Prophet ﷺ saying: the days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking (Sahih Muslim 1141). Because of this, fasting on those days is generally not allowed, with a narrow exception reported for pilgrims who could not afford a sacrificial animal; ask a scholar about your case.\n\nThey are also days of remembering Allah, as Allah says: remember Allah during the numbered days (Qur\'an 2:203).\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 1141; Qur\'an 2:203.\n[GO:/calendar]',
